INT. BASALT CAVERN OF THE MOON-WELL - NIGHT

A vaulted cave. A pool of still, silver water at its center, lit from below. Stalactites drip in a slow rhythm. Runes glow faintly on the walls.

PRINCESS LYSANDRA OYELOWO-VANE (20s, travel-worn gown, a sword at her hip) kneels at the pool's edge, cupping silver water in her hands. She lets it spill through her fingers.

LYSANDRA
(to herself)
Tell me the way. Tell me the way home.

The water ripples. A glimmer rises from the depths and shivers into a voice.

MORGWYN (V.O.)
(whispering)
Seek the king's lost daughter.

LYSANDRA
I am the king's lost daughter.

MORGWYN (V.O.)
(whispering)
Then seek the one who kept you.

A pebble clatters down the cave wall. Lysandra rises, sword half-drawn. From the shadows steps a woman in a hooded gray cloak. MORGWYN ASHWORTH-ABARA (50s, silver hair, a staff of white ash). She lowers her hood.

MORGWYN
Hello, child.

LYSANDRA
Morgwyn?

MORGWYN
You've grown.

LYSANDRA
You vanished.

MORGWYN
I was told to.

LYSANDRA
By whom?

MORGWYN
By the king.

LYSANDRA
He lied to us both.

^MORGWYN
He lied to us both.

They stare at each other, startled by the echo. The silver water stills.

LYSANDRA
Then who is she? The one who sits on my throne?

MORGWYN
She is your sister.

LYSANDRA
I have no sister.

MORGWYN
You do now. And she is waiting.

Lysandra sheathes her sword. She wipes her hand on her gown and steps toward Morgwyn, who lifts the staff and draws a circle in the air. The circle opens on a green meadow, full of light.
